WEBVTT

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.970
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.210
Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!! Guts!! Gobble!!

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:39.050
Calling everything delicious!

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:43.550
The more I eat, the more powerful I get!

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.920
Let’s capture ingredients around the world!

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.500
I dream of being an invincible 
Gourmet Fighter!!

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:56.530
Now on to the bottom of the 
sea, or the tops of glaciers!

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.200
Jump! Jump Jump Jump! 
Knock! Knock Knock Knock!

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.400
Give thanks!

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.610
Let’s eat!

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.410
Wow wo!! Spiked Punch! Wow wo!! Multi-fold!

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:15.550
Guts! Gutsy Guts! I can eat any dream!

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.820
Wow wo!! My very own... 
Wow wo!! ...Full Course!

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.990
Guts! Gutsy Guts! Gather them all up!

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:31.070
And put the world on my plate!

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.870
Wow wow wow! Eat the mountains!!

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.440
Wow wow wow! Toriko!!

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.040
Wow wow wow! Eat the oceans!!

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.310
Wow wow wow! Tori, Tori, Tori, Toriko!!

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:50.990
Someone once said...

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:56.460
There are carp with scales 
made of casino coins,

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.430
and after eating their delicious meat, 
you can gamble with their scales!

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:05.000
Coin Carp!

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:10.340
If you cut this kind of 
watermelon with a knife,

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:14.110
its giant seeds will look 
like the numbers on a die...

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:19.150
Diced Watermelon!

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.350
The world is in the Gourmet Age...

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:29.660
An age in which people quest for 
yet unknown culinary delights!

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:36.200
While on the hunt for Meteor Garlic,

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.930
the next ingredient ordered by the president,

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:40.430
Toriko and company got caught 
up in a concentration-like game

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:43.500
of Gourmet Tasting with Livebearer,

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.840
where the stakes are memories of eating!

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:49.740
Toriko-san! They may disappear!

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:53.680
Your memories... All of 
your delicious memories...

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:55.480
The past doesn't matter.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.550
We've only got our eyes on the future.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:01.920
And I'm talking all the time!

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.620
I'll explain the rules.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.260
Two cards are turned over.

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.290
The person who gets a matching pair

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:12.630
has to eat the same food that's on the cards.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.230
After the ingredient is devoured,

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:17.970
the person gets the number of 
points that are on the card.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.410
You match cards, eat a bunch of food,

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.810
and at the end, the player with 
the most points wins, right?

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:29.880
Toriko and Livebearer matched, then ate, 
one pair of ingredients after another.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:33.420
After two turns, Toriko's 
team, which went first,

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.090
has a total of 310 points.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.620
Livebearer has 220 points.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:43.690
The game is heating up, with 
neither side willing to back down!

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:47.000
I'm definitely going to steal it from him!

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.500
I'll swipe the contents of that golden brain!

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.500
It's my turn, isn't it?

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.810
Now the real game begins.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:05.150
Coco's Gambit! The Ingredients 
that Determine Victory or Defeat!

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.690
Alright, Livebearer-sama got 
a hit with a Rockadillo!

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:21.460
If he can eat it, he'll obtain 70 points!

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:25.270
However, his Beast opponent 
boasts a Capture Level of 60!

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.170
That's some kinda strong!

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:31.140
If he can't eat the whole thing, 
we get those 70 points, right?

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.140
Hi there!

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:36.610
There we go!

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:40.380
Damn, he's strong!

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:53.800
Livebearer-sama has successfully 
devoured the ingredient!

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.300
He gets 70 points!

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.370
Number 9 and number 50.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:04.670
Another match!

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:08.380
A 150-point River Styx Poison Lizard!

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.380
It's a poisonous Special 
Preparation Ingredient!

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:24.890
In you go...

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:26.830
A little more...

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.530
First a Rockadillo, now a 
River Styx Poison Lizard...

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:37.940
He also effortlessly prepared and 
ate the River Styx Poison Lizard!

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.810
That's 150 points!

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:43.140
There it is! A lucky card!

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.210
Garlic Crab, a 200-point match!

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:48.580
Not only can he eat it with ease,

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:50.620
it's a lucky card worth lots of points!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.720
First the Melon Egg, now this...

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.320
How can it be this easy for 
him to draw lucky cards?!

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:59.130
Bastard... That's another turn with 
consecutive high point cards...

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:02.260
He knows exactly what all 
the cards are and where...

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:05.060
But what the hell kind of trick is he using?!

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:09.140
Steaming is the best way 
to go with Garlic Crabs.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.280
Livebearer-sama has polished it off!

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.410
He gets 200 points!

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:24.620
He achieved 420 points this 
turn for a total of 640 points!

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:27.690
Th-That man is amazing...

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.060
Never mind the lucky cards.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:33.590
Apart from those, all the ingredients 
he's had were hard to capture or prepare.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:36.560
Especially the River Styx Poison Lizard...

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:39.660
Removing the poison from it 
takes considerable technique.

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:42.530
It has to be kept at an 
exactly 80 degree boil

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:45.240
while the poison is skimmed 
off with the scum.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:48.510
His skill as a chef is the real thing!

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.970
Naturally.

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:53.980
Although it's really just a collection 
of skills I stole from many chefs...

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.050
I can't wait to suck out

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:01.920
various goodies from your brain!

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.860
With three hits and three 
meals eaten in a row,

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.020
it becomes the other side's turn!

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:09.160
Coco! I'm countin' on you to 
get us high point cards too!

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.800
No matter what it is, I'll 
eat it from stem to stern!

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:17.430
This game...

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:20.300
At a glance, it looks like 
a battle for points...

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:23.870
But thinking about the flow of the 
game so far, I realize that's wrong.

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:25.680
It's the opposite of the lucky cards...

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:29.010
The key is avoiding the unlucky cards.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:33.580
Though the game is like concentration, 
there are numbers on back of the cards,

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:36.850
put there on purpose to make it easy to 
remember the location of ingredients.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:39.020
In other words, for this game,

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.390
getting frequent hits is part of the premise.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:45.230
Number 5!

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:47.660
Oh, no!

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:51.330
Number 5 is an Electric Banana! 
A narcotic ingredient!

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.500
Here we go. An illegal ingredient...

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:57.540
Number 54!

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.540
That's an Atlas Crab!

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.710
You're out!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:06.210
This is the first "out" in 
the game for either team!

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.380
The turn goes back to Livebearer-sama!

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:09.420
Coco!

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.350
Coco-san!

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:18.930
He went out on purpose...

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:22.300
Did he make a mistake with the first card?

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:27.100
Or did he just do it to find out 
the kind of ingredients and points?

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:28.300
Either way,

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:32.870
even if you know where the matches 
are, you've revealed to me

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.040
that you don't know what's on the cards.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:39.310
Your reason for going as far as 
missing on the second card...

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:43.980
It seems you understand the point of 
this game, Coco of the Four Kings.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:45.050
That's right...

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:49.890
Indeed, the key of the game is not 
dropping out in the middle of it.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:54.290
The cause of defeat for every team 
that's challenged me thus far

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:57.960
wasn't a lesser amount of points 
after all the cards were drawn.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:02.700
All of them have quit during the 
game after drawing an unlucky card.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.040
You saw the first card was an Electric Banana

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.870
and predicted it would be difficult to eat,

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.780
so you purposely avoided getting a match.

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:12.480
Still, even after realizing that,

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:15.550
your chances of winning are zero!

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:19.790
I'm wearing trick contact lenses!

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:25.060
All of the Gourmet Casino cards 
are specially constructed.

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:31.660
When I look at them with these lenses, 
a 3D image of the card face pops out.

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:34.030
Lucky and unlucky cards, too...

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:37.840
They're all as plain as day to me!

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:41.970
Alright, here's a chance 
to widen the point gap!

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:44.280
It's Livebearer-sama's third turn!

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:46.280
Number 28...

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:47.680
And number 45!

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:52.880
Livebearer-sama got a match 
with the 60-point Rock Potato!

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:55.350
Numbers 14 and 39!

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:59.920
Continuing with a Brain Urchin! 
That's a 30-point hit!

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:02.030
Numbers 10 and 17!

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:07.030
Oh, my! Yet another lucky card! Shock Lemon!

00:10:07.030 --> 00:10:08.870
That's a 200-point hit!

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.370
Livebearer-sama is unrelenting!

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:27.950
Livebearer-sama has achieved 
290 points this turn!

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.820
His total is 930 points!

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:35.660
The Coco-Toriko-Komatsu team still 
has a total of just 310 points!

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:38.190
The gap between them is even wider!

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.800
And now it's the Coco-Toriko-Komatsu 
team's turn!

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:42.430
Number 51!

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:47.640
Oh, my! Number 51 is Dragonfire!

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.340
Dragonfire?!

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.310
That's another tough ingredient to eat!

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:55.480
Number 19.

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:58.880
Oh, no! Number 19 is a Rock Lizard!

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:00.180
Out again!

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:00.980
Coco!

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:01.920
Coco-san!

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:04.790
What's wrong, Coco-Toriko-Komatsu team?!

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:08.890
It seems he really doesn't 
know what's on the cards...

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:12.630
Okay! Time for me to win this!

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.270
Flavor Ant! A 40-point hit!

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:19.330
Bubble Abalone! A 20 point-hit!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:22.100
Oh my goodness! Yet another lucky card!

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:25.340
Golden Shrimp, a 200-point hit!

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:28.140
A wave of hits!

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:34.880
Livebearer-sama receives 
260 points this turn!

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:38.190
His total is 1,190 points!

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:43.120
That's 880 points more than 
the Coco-Toriko-Komatsu team!

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.860
There are ten ingredients left!

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:50.160
Things don't look good for 
the Coco-Toriko-Komatsu team!

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:52.700
We're gonna be in real trouble 
if he pulls ahead any more!

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.870
Coco-san!

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:59.570
Since the start of the game, he's 
been able to efficiently gain points.

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:01.440
He's seen me go out twice,

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:04.340
and matched up the lucky cards haphazardly.

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:06.980
Now we're getting to the heart of it.

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:10.420
The cards that he intentionally avoided...

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.820
I presume they're the 
unluckiest cards of all.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:16.490
That's where we have a chance to win!

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.850
The cards that he intentionally avoided...

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:43.420
I presume they're the 
unluckiest cards of all.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:45.480
That's where we have a chance to win!

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:47.350
That, and the order of turns.

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:49.220
Number one, please!

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:53.230
Atlas Crab for 30 points!

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:55.960
That's the ingredient that showed up before!

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.700
We'll take this one.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.930
Toriko, Komatsu-kun, I'm counting on you.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:01.570
Number 54!

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:06.000
Number 54! Atlas Crab! It's a match!

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:17.320
Alright! Leave it to me!

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:23.320
Flying Fork!

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:24.890
What?!

00:13:28.090 --> 00:13:30.960
18-fold Spiked Punch!

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.100
That ate a lot of time...

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.870
Preparing the thing's in your hands, Komatsu!

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:44.540
Right! You can count on me!

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:53.850
Atlas Crab dressed with chili sauce!

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:56.250
It looks delicious!

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:58.860
Coating it with honey after boiling

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:00.120
makes the meat tender

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:03.560
and the chili sauce makes the 
whole thing glisten beautifully!

00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:04.690
Go ahead!

00:14:05.260 --> 00:14:08.730
I give thanks for all of 
this world's bounty...

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:10.830
Time to dig in!

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:15.470
Delicious!

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:17.740
Thank you for the meal!

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:19.410
Successfully eaten!

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:21.680
They gain 30 points!

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:24.580
But he's still way ahead of us...

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:26.180
We're in a tight spot, aren't we?

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:28.380
Keep goin', Coco!

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:32.820
There are less than ten ingredients left.

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:35.890
The skull images I see 
coming off of five pairs...

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:38.460
He's avoiding those cards, too.

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:40.960
I have to confirm it.

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:42.900
Number 21!

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.940
T-That's...

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:49.570
...Poison Potato!

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:52.270
There it is! An unlucky card!

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:54.180
Poison Potato?!

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:57.210
This is a Super-Special 
Preparation Ingredient!

00:14:57.210 --> 00:15:00.480
No one has ever successfully 
removed its poison!

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.350
It's a mega-poisonous potato!

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:04.620
P-Poison Potato?!

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:07.820
There's no record of even 
Setsuno-san detoxifying it!

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:11.030
Then it can't be eaten?

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:12.460
Yeah. It's impossible.

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:16.860
It's said the Poison Potato is 20 times 
more poisonous than the Puffer Whale.

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:20.370
I don't even have the 
antibody for its poison.

00:15:20.570 --> 00:15:23.470
And it's only worth ten points!

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:26.470
Getting out the poison, then eating 
it in ten minutes just isn't possible!

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:29.280
That certainly is an unlucky ingredient!

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:34.510
Oh dear, that is one nasty ingredient...

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:37.020
I wanna stay away from it too.

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:41.890
Wait. Number 24, please.

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:46.260
Don't tell me he's tryin' 
to get a hit with that...

00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:49.100
What's this?! A joker card!

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:51.900
And moreover, it's another Super-Special 
Preparation Ingredient!

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:53.500
Nitro Cherries!

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.840
N-Nitro Cherries?!

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:59.410
Cherries that detonate with 
even the slightest prodding!

00:16:01.510 --> 00:16:03.580
It's an extremely dangerous ingredient

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:07.310
that explodes inside the body after 
consumption if it's not prepared correctly!

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:11.180
And this card is only ten points too!

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:13.120
It's not only unlucky, it's a joker card!

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:14.890
Joker card?!

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:16.290
This is the first time one's come up!

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:17.360
Yeah.

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:20.930
If you eat it, apparently you get to trade

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:23.060
one of your cards with your opponent's cards.

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:26.360
If we could switch, it would 
decrease the point gap.

00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:30.500
But even if we get a hit with Nitro 
Cherries, eating them's a tough feat.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:33.910
The Coco-Toriko-Komatsu team is out!

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:35.310
It's now Livebearer-sama's turn!

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:40.440
At last, it's gotten difficult 
to choose cards, you know?

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:41.980
Number 18, if you please.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:46.080
Number 18! Hanya Panda!

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:49.250
That's another one! A joker card!

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:50.990
H-Hanya Panda?!

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:54.120
It's a Beast that makes you let down 
your guard with its panda-like look

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:56.790
and then suddenly attacks!

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:58.660
Capture Level 80...

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.000
They had a Beast like this prepared, too?!

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:05.670
However, the Hanya Panda 
is a 250-point ingredient.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:09.540
It's a joker with points befitting 
the difficulty of its Capture Level!

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:11.710
Sounds like a pain.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:13.340
Number 12!

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.380
Number 12! Troll Cheese!

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:20.420
That's an out! It's the other side's turn.

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:22.220
Troll Cheese...

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:26.220
It's a cheese that gives off such a 
powerful stench, you can't even breathe!

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:28.490
It's a totally inedible ingredient!

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:30.430
And it's ten points?!

00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:32.430
That's an unlucky card!

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:36.130
He didn't get a hit with the joker card, huh?

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:38.530
He's leading in points by a wide margin.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:43.670
It isn't worth it for him to fight 
a Hanya Panda just to trade cards.

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:47.210
More importantly, Troll Cheese...

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.040
And Hanya Panda...

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:50.510
Number 11!

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:53.680
Number 11! Urchin Rat!

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:56.150
It's got a high Capture Level, 
but is worth ten points!

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:57.990
This is also an unlucky card!

00:17:58.320 --> 00:17:59.290
Number 27!

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:03.320
Number 27! Scissor Snake! Out!

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:05.460
And that's an unlucky card, too!

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:07.000
It's the other side's turn!

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:11.170
Even though the Capture Level of Urchin 
Rats and Scissor Snakes is over 50,

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:12.230
they're worth ten points!

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:15.170
And now, all cards have appeared!

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:19.240
None of the remaining cards 
are gonna be an easy job!

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:21.940
Whatever the ingredient, if we get a hit,

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:24.310
will I be able to prepare it?

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:30.250
There are nine pairs left.

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:32.890
850 points separating us from him...

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:36.190
To turn the tables on him from here on...

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:40.090
Numbers 11 and 21, please.

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:42.700
Urchin Rat!

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:44.000
Poison Potato!

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:45.130
Out!

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:46.270
It's the other side's turn!

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:48.400
He went out on purpose?!

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:51.800
I knew it! He's got a big 
edge when it comes to points.

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:53.740
He's not gonna put himself 
in danger needlessly.

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:56.180
Whoever gets ten outs first loses.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:58.410
Coco and them got an out first.

00:18:58.810 --> 00:19:01.550
If they keep getting outs 
like this, they'll lose.

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:04.950
Anyway, they need to get a match or else...

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:23.200
Toriko!

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:25.440
We're going for broke!

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:26.740
About time!

00:19:27.270 --> 00:19:29.270
Numbers 18 and 35!

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.340
Hanya Panda! A match!

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:32.980
It's all you!

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:33.910
Yeah!

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:37.680
Beasts that have a Capture Level over 60

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:41.150
are kept in an underground stockroom!

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:15.420
Been a while since I've 
had a tough opponent...

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:18.720
This'll be a perfect start 
to turning this thing around!

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:21.860
True...

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:26.500
The only way you can come from 
behind is by using a joker.

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:29.800
Komatsu-kun...

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:31.030
I need to talk to you.

00:20:55.620 --> 00:20:58.230
In those younger days,

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.130
No matter how you chased them,

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:04.730
The sky-spanning rainbows got away

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:08.040
After that, time passed

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:10.510
Were you able to grasp

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:15.140
The rainbow by the name of dreams then?

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:18.850
When it comes to a new challenge,

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:24.090
You turn into a coward,

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:29.560
But your chance ain't gonna wait on you,

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:34.430
So now's the time!

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:42.100
Bet those tears and that kindness

00:21:42.100 --> 00:21:46.370
Will light up tomorrow

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:49.440
That's right, rainbows are 
all the more beautiful

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:53.250
Because we can't catch 'em

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:57.050
Today's Gourmet Tasting Lecture!

00:21:57.680 --> 00:21:59.250
I'm your newscaster, Tina.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:01.220
We've got a heated Gourmet Tasting showdown!

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:04.190
In this segment, I'll give you 
a heaping helping of commentary

00:22:04.190 --> 00:22:07.060
on today's game and its important points!

00:22:08.290 --> 00:22:10.630
When we started this week,

00:22:10.630 --> 00:22:13.730
Livebearer had 220 points and 
Toriko's team had 310 points.

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:17.400
While Toriko's team kept going out,

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:21.040
Livebearer got one hit after 
another and devoured them all!

00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:24.180
His total is now 1,190 points!

00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:26.050
Toriko's team is in a pinch!

00:22:26.280 --> 00:22:28.480
But Coco figured it out!

00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:32.150
Actually, this Gourmet Tasting 
isn't a battle over points,

00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:34.390
but whether you can avoid the unlucky cards!

00:22:34.390 --> 00:22:37.820
The key to winning is not dropping out!

00:22:37.820 --> 00:22:40.090
The cards are laid out! The 
remaining ingredients...

00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:41.990
...are all difficult to eat!

00:22:41.990 --> 00:22:44.460
There's an 850-point gap 
between the two sides!

00:22:44.460 --> 00:22:47.130
And Toriko's team is striking back at last!

00:22:47.470 --> 00:22:49.870
They got a hit with the Hanya Panda card!

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:52.340
And here's today's cool point!

00:22:54.610 --> 00:22:58.610
Hanya Panda is a tough Beast 
with a Capture Level of 80!

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:01.910
Will Toriko be able to beat 
and eat the Hanya Panda?!

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:04.450
What'll happen next in the Gourmet Tasting?!

00:23:07.050 --> 00:23:10.120
Toriko takes on a violent beast!

00:23:10.120 --> 00:23:13.620
What is Coco's plan to deal with this onslaught of challenges?

00:23:14.120 --> 00:23:16.860
Eat or Be Eaten! Toriko vs. Hanya Panda!

00:23:17.200 --> 00:23:18.930
Look forward to another heaping helping of fun!
